  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is config_002: RNA-only, multiprofile, PCA, avgpool, with validation accuracy 0.5907 and F1 0.5727, clearly better than single-profile PCA and transformer aggregation, while image-only ResNet is weak. The key uncertainty is whether a learned RNA representation can improve the best known profile/aggregation setting. config_005 changes only the RNA encoder to scvi_n200 while keeping multiprofile and avgpool fixed, directly isolating the effect of representation. This is a controlled exploitation of the most promising current direction and avoids confounding the result with image modality or fusion, making it the most informative next experiment under a limited budget."
